Libraries from outside the project the programs use: the versions, where they came from and how they were fetched.

DXVK 3.1.1 (zlib/libpng licence: external/dxvk/LICENSE): Direct3D 9 for the Linux program, libdxvk_d3d9.so on Vulkan,
in external/dxvk.

Source: https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk, tag v3.1.1 (commit b1a1c99ab52b687cf950d62c88bc2fa316b41663) with its
submodules include/native/directx (mingw-directx-headers 9df86f2341616ef1888ae59919feaa6d4fad693d),
subprojects/dxbc-spirv (bf14419e5fa7eacb817b7b632f03cb61d61bbad7) and subprojects/libdisplay-info
(275e6459c7ab1ddd4b125f28d0440716e4888078):

    git clone --depth 1 --branch v3.1.1 --recurse-submodules --shallow-submodules https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk

copied without the git files and without three header submodules: include/vulkan (Vulkan-Headers: the build takes
the system's, as DXVK's meson.build does when the folder is absent), include/spirv (SPIRV-Headers) and all of
subprojects/dxbc-spirv/submodules/spirv_headers but its LICENSE and the two headers the build reads
(include/spirv/unified1/spirv.hpp and GLSL.std.450.h, which serve both). No file is changed.

cmake/Dxvk.cmake builds it with Meson (only Direct3D 9, SDL3 as the window system) using the program's own compilers,
and the program links the result; the build machine needs meson, glslang and the Vulkan headers. At run time it needs
DXVK_WSI_DRIVER=SDL3 (no default off Windows; harness/run.sh -L sets it): DXVK then opens libSDL3.so.0, which is the
program's own shared SDL3 (external/SDL3, shared on Linux), and takes the game's HWND as the SDL_Window*. The game's
src/SDK/DirectX/d3d9.h, not DXVK's headers, declares what the program calls; only harness/tools/adapter.cpp
(run.sh -L's adapter probe) is built on DXVK's headers.

libogg 1.3.6 and libvorbis 1.3.7 (Xiph.Org, BSD licence: external/ogg/COPYING, external/vorbis/COPYING): Ogg Vorbis
decoding for every program (the game's voice and sound files), in external/ogg and external/vorbis.

Source: Xiph.Org's release tarballs, https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/ogg/libogg-1.3.6.tar.gz (sha256
83e6704730683d004d20e21b8f7f55dcb3383cdf84c0daedf30bde175f774638) and
https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/vorbis/libvorbis-1.3.7.tar.gz (sha256
0e982409a9c3fc82ee06e08205b1355e5c6aa4c36bca58146ef399621b0ce5ab), the hashes of the SHA256SUMS files beside them:

    curl -fsSLO https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/ogg/libogg-1.3.6.tar.gz
    curl -fsSLO https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/vorbis/libvorbis-1.3.7.tar.gz
    sha256sum libogg-1.3.6.tar.gz libvorbis-1.3.7.tar.gz
    tar -xzf libogg-1.3.6.tar.gz && tar -xzf libvorbis-1.3.7.tar.gz

Kept, unchanged: from libogg, AUTHORS, COPYING, README.md, include/ogg/{ogg.h,os_types.h,config_types.h.in} and
src/{bitwise.c,framing.c,crctable.h}; from libvorbis, AUTHORS, COPYING, include/vorbis/{codec.h,vorbisfile.h},
lib/*.h and the sources of upstream's libvorbis and libvorbisfile (lib/*.c without vorbisenc.c, barkmel.c, psytune.c
and tone.c). Left out: the encoder library (vorbisenc.c, vorbisenc.h, lib/modes, lib/books), the tools, docs,
examples, tests and build scripts. CMake builds them as the static library xfnv_vorbis (CMakeLists.txt), writing
libogg's config_types.h from config_types.h.in as upstream's configure does; the game includes
<vorbis/vorbisfile.h> (src/BSAudio/BSWin32GameSound.h).

minimp3 (lieff, CC0 1.0: external/minimp3/LICENSE): MP3 decoding for the music the game plays through DirectShow
(src/platform/dsound/DirectShowDecoder.cpp, the only file that includes it). Header-only.

Source: https://github.com/lieff/minimp3, commit a2ad968c94819fb98589cca8026e0a57958c963c:

    git clone https://github.com/lieff/minimp3 && git -C minimp3 checkout a2ad968c94819fb98589cca8026e0a57958c963c

Kept, unchanged: minimp3.h, minimp3_ex.h and LICENSE. Left out: the tests, fuzzers, player and scripts.

doctest 2.4.11 (Viktor Kirilov, MIT licence: external/doctest/LICENSE.txt): the unit test framework of the programs in
tests/ (tests/README.md). Header-only.

Source: https://github.com/doctest/doctest, tag v2.4.11, its single-header release:

    curl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/doctest/doctest/v2.4.11/doctest/doctest.h
    curl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/doctest/doctest/v2.4.11/LICENSE.txt

Kept, unchanged: doctest.h (sha256 44faa038e9c3f9728efbda143748d01124ea0a27f4bf78f35a15d8fab2e039fb) and LICENSE.txt.
